          "kicker": "Coaching backing",
          "heading": "Former Bulls staff back Jake White to make Fiji surprise people",
          "body": "Jake White's former colleagues at Loftus Versfeld reckon Fiji have the right man, with ex-Bulls backline coach Chris Rossouw suggesting they could surprise people. White, 62, replaces interim coach Senirusi Seruvakula and inherits a side ranked 10th that has lost four of five Tests this year. Bulls CEO Edgar Rathbone, quoted by Rapport, credits White with high-performance structures, and Willem Strauss says he leaves teams in better shape. His first match is Japan this Saturday."
