          "kicker": "Red Roses setback",
          "heading": "Women's: England's 41-match unbeaten run ends as Canada win 24-21 in Toronto",
          "body": "England women's 41-match unbeaten run, stretching back almost four years, ended in Toronto as Shoshanah Seumanutafa's late try gave Canada a 24-21 win in the WXV Global Series. Canada are the first side to beat England since November 2022, when New Zealand won the World Cup final. Head coach John Mitchell said: \"We're disappointed by the result but there was some very good things in our performance. So we'll stick to our processes.\" The rematch in Ottawa comes before the series finishes against the USA in New Jersey."
