          "body": "Les Kiss was shell-shocked after the Wallabies' Bledisloe II humbling, saying of the first half: 'None of us accept 22-0.' Australia trailed 36-7 at half-time and lost 43-21 at Accor Stadium, their 13th straight defeat to New Zealand. Kiss's side had been unbeaten through six Tests, including a win over world No 1 South Africa last month, until Eden Park. The Guardian's Angus Fontaine says the honeymoon is over."
