          "heading": "Beauden Barrett, Damian McKenzie praised by New Zealand media after Sydney win",
          "body": "New Zealand's rugby writers were lavish after Saturday's second Bledisloe Test, a 43-21 win in Sydney that the New Zealand Herald's Gregor Paul called \"about as good as it gets from the All Blacks\". Damian McKenzie, shifted from full-back to fly-half for the first Test, and Beauden Barrett, who \"wound back the clock\", were among those praised, while Codie Taylor's captain's innings was singled out too. Paul also gave special praise to Dave Rennie's \"vision\" for the All Blacks. New Zealand led 36-7 at half-time."
