          "heading": "Club: Lions honour Hyron Andrews with tearful tribute before Champions Cup opener",
          "body": "Club news: South Africa's Lions paid an emotional tribute to Hyron Andrews, the 31-year-old who was found unresponsive at the team hotel on Île de Ré on Friday, hours before their European Champions Cup opener. Players could not hold back tears during a silent observance, his number five shirt laid in front of the team and his jersey number left vacant. The Lions lost 31-14 at La Rochelle, and although South Africa Rugby said he died after falling at the hotel, no official cause of death has been confirmed."
